# Quilt name leaderboard — go public (Phase 2)

Today the leaderboard is **admin-only** (`openQuiltNameLeaderboard` in admin menu). The quilt screen still uses the old AI word-cloud ballot (`mountPublicQuiltNameBallot`).

Before making the leaderboard public, complete **all** of this:

## 1. Railway cutoff cron (required for public)

Lazy cutoff (on first leaderboard load/vote after 15:00 UTC) is fine for admin preview. **Not** fine once real users vote.

- Add a **second Railway cron service** (same pattern as `daily-reset-cron`)
- Config-as-code: `railway.quilt-name-leaderboard-finalize.json`
- Schedule: `0 15 * * *` (15:00 UTC ≈ 10 AM CT)
- Start command: `node scripts/trigger-quilt-name-leaderboard-finalize.cjs`
- Env: `RESET_TOKEN` + `RESET_URL` (or `QUILT_NAME_LEADERBOARD_FINALIZE_URL`)
- See `docs/railway-daily-reset-cron.md` for the same setup pattern

## 2. Wire quilt screen

- Replace `mountPublicQuiltNameBallot` on `screen-quilt` with leaderboard UI (`ui-service.js`)
- Use `Utils.getTodayKey()` for `dateKey` (not local calendar date)
- Remove or hide `#quiltNameBallotWrap` old 20-word cloud

## 3. Retire old ballot path

- Stop using `/api/quilt-name-generate` elimination flow for public UI
- Single vote path: `/api/quilt-name-leaderboard-vote` + `entries[]` on `quiltNames/{dateKey}`
- `winningQuiltName` still feeds IG carousel / nightly job — contract unchanged

## 4. Defaults (locked unless product asks otherwise)

- **8-hour** submission window (07:00–15:00 UTC)
- **Single vote** per device, changeable during voting
- **AI fallback** only if &lt;5 names at cutoff
- **Accept all** unique community names (no fixed cap; ~50 safety limit)

## Smoke before ship

```bash
RESET_URL=https://our-daily-quilt-production.up.railway.app/api/daily-reset \
RESET_TOKEN=your-token \
node scripts/trigger-quilt-name-leaderboard-finalize.cjs
```

Expect HTTP 200 and `"phase": "voting"`.
